<p id="S3.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">The conditions for a complete O’Nan configuration in unital <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a,b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a,b}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)=(1,b_{0}+b_{1}\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)=(1,b_{0}+b_{1}\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> are (using the notation as described in Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Field properties for even 𝑞 ‣ 2 Buekenhout-Metz unitals ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>).</span></p>
