<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note if we fix <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,h\in\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,h\in\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the first two equations determines <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=k_{0}+k_{1}\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=k_{0}+k_{1}\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> depend linearly on <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the LHS of (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) are fixed linear expressions in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and, as <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+k^{q}=k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+k^{q}=k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) determines <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and using (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), since <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{kh}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{kh}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{F}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>-coefficient of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> of the expression for <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kh</annotation></semantics></math>, </span><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text"> <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}h_{1}+k_{1}h_{0}+k_{1}h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}h_{1}+k_{1}h_{0}+k_{1}h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, this determines <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now suppose the above configuration, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,b,x,k,h,s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,b,x,k,h,s,t)</annotation></semantics></math>, is a complete BM-special Fano plane, and so the above equations hold. We will define a configuration in <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,b^{\prime},x^{\prime},k^{\prime},h,s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,b^{\prime},x^{\prime},k^{\prime},h,s,t)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xk=x^{\prime}k^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xk=x^{\prime}k^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and show that it is a complete BM-special Fano plane in <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The configuration <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> has the points <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y,V</annotation></semantics></math> in common with the configuration in <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a,b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a,b}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}=(x^{\prime}k^{\prime}h,k^{\prime}h,1)=(\theta h,k^{\prime}h,1)\quad Q^{\prime}=(x^{\prime}k^{\prime},k^{\prime},1)=(\theta,k^{\prime},1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}=(x^{\prime}k^{\prime}h,k^{\prime}h,1)=(\theta h,k^{\prime}h,1)\quad Q^{\prime}=(x^{\prime}k^{\prime},k^{\prime},1)=(\theta,k^{\prime},1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}=(\theta W,k^{\prime}W+U,1),\quad N^{\prime}=(\theta V,k^{\prime}V+Z,1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}=(\theta W,k^{\prime}W+U,1),\quad N^{\prime}=(\theta V,k^{\prime}V+Z,1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">(Note that <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W,U,V,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W,U,V,Z</annotation></semantics></math> only involve <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h,s,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h,s,t</annotation></semantics></math> which are fixed for the two scenarios <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a,b},{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a,b},{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We require that the following equations hold for the configuration to be a Fano plane in <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{(\theta h)^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}(\theta h)^{q+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></menclose><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{(\theta h)^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}(\theta h)^{q+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{\theta^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}\theta^{q+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></menclose><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{\theta^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}\theta^{q+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{(\theta W)^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}(\theta W)^{q+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></menclose><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{(\theta W)^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}(\theta W)^{q+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}W}+\boxed{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></menclose><mo>+</mo><menclose notation="box"><mi>U</mi></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}W}+\boxed{U}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{(\theta V)^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}(\theta V)^{q+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></menclose><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{(\theta V)^{2}}+b_{1}^{\prime}(\theta V)^{q+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}V}+\boxed{Z}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></menclose><mo>+</mo><menclose notation="box"><mi>Z</mi></menclose></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{k^{\prime}V}+\boxed{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">As before (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) determine <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we define <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}=\theta/k^{\prime}=xk/k^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}=\theta/k^{\prime}=xk/k^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) hold and express that points <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime},Q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime},Q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of the configuration lie in <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence we need to show that (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) hold.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start with (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). As (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) holds, it is sufficient to show that (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) holds, that is</span></p>
