</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is equal to LHS (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Number of BM-special Fano planes ‣ 3 Main results for BM-unitals, even 𝑞 ‣ A Note on Fano Planes in Orthogonal Buekenhout-Metz Unitals of Even Order" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), as required, showing that <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The argument for <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{a^{\prime},b^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is similar. Thus we have shown that <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y,V,P^{\prime},Q^{\prime},M^{\prime},N^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y,V,P^{\prime},Q^{\prime},M^{\prime},N^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> form a BM-special Fano plane.
Thus there is a correspondence between BM-special Fano planes in the two unitals and so the two unitals contain the same number of BM-special Fano planes.
∎</span></p>
</div>
