<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Tits Unitals</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Discussion</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Feng and Li <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> also show the existence of O’Nan configurations in Tits unitals. We have investigated their constructions and in some, but not all, cases, their construction can be completed to a Fano plane contained within the Tits unital. In particular, for <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;2048</annotation></semantics></math>, our Magma <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> calculations report that for each appropriate value of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> there is at least one such Fano plane, with the exception of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=128</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Examples</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Tits unital has infinite point <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math> and finite points, for <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x_{0}+x_{1}\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x_{0}+x_{1}\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0},x_{1},r\in\mathbb{F}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0},x_{1},r\in\mathbb{F}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{x,r}=(x_{0}+x_{1}\delta,\ r+f(x_{0},x_{1})\delta,1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{x,r}=(x_{0}+x_{1}\delta,\ r+f(x_{0},x_{1})\delta,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)=x^{\tau+1}+xy+y^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)=x^{\tau+1}+xy+y^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=2^{2m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=2^{2m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is an odd power of 2, following Feng and Li <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> we suppose <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in{\mbox{F}}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mtext>F</mtext><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in{\mbox{F}}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{2}=\delta+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{2}=\delta+1</annotation></semantics></math>, further <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{q}=\delta+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{q}=\delta+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\colon\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}\rightarrow\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}},\quad\tau\colon x\mapsto x^{2^{m+1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\colon\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}\rightarrow\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}},\quad\tau\colon x\mapsto x^{2^{m+1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so if <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{F}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{F}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\tau^{2}}=x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\tau^{2}}=x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here we give an example of a Fano plane contained in the Tits unital obtained by extending the Feng and Li construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Example 1</span></span><span id="Thmexample1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=8</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=2^{2m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=2^{2m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\colon x\mapsto x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\colon x\mapsto x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is a generator of <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{F}_{q}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_{q}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{7}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{7}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{3}=w+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{3}=w+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=w^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=w^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=w^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=w^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we have <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=(0,0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=(0,0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}=(0,w^{2},1),\ \ R_{2}=(0,w^{5},1),\ \ P=(1,e+w,1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}=(0,w^{2},1),\ \ R_{2}=(0,w^{5},1),\ \ P=(1,e+w,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=(w^{5}+w^{6}\delta,w^{6}+\delta,1),\ \ P_{2}=(w^{3}+w^{6}\delta,w^{4}+\delta,1),\ \ M=(w^{3}+w^{5}\delta,1+\delta,1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=(w^{5}+w^{6}\delta,w^{6}+\delta,1),\ \ P_{2}=(w^{3}+w^{6}\delta,w^{4}+\delta,1),\ \ M=(w^{3}+w^{5}\delta,1+\delta,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We can check that <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, by calculating</p>
<table id="S4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w^{5},w^{6})=(w^{5})^{4+2}+w^{5}w^{6}+(w^{6})^{4}=w^{30}+w^{11}+w^{24}=w^{2}+w^{4}+w^{3}=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>30</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>24</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w^{5},w^{6})=(w^{5})^{4+2}+w^{5}w^{6}+(w^{6})^{4}=w^{30}+w^{11}+w^{24}=w^{2}+w^{4}+w^{3}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">using <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{3}=w+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{3}=w+1</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{4}=w^{2}+w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{4}=w^{2}+w</annotation></semantics></math>. Looking at the <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> part of the second coordinate <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{6}+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{6}+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, this is 1, so this confirms that <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly for <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now check <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w^{3},w^{5})=w^{18}+w^{8}+w^{20}=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>18</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>20</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w^{3},w^{5})=w^{18}+w^{8}+w^{20}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">as required. This shows that the points all lie on <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and it is easy to check they form a Fano plane.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Example 2</span></span><span id="Thmexample2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmexample2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose now that <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=32</annotation></semantics></math>. We choose a generator <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mbox{F}}_{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>F</mtext><mn>32</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mbox{F}}_{32}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{5}=w^{2}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{5}=w^{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Her we have <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=w^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=w^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}=w^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}=w^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\colon x\mapsto x^{2^{3}}=x^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\colon x\mapsto x^{2^{3}}=x^{8}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}=(0,w^{4},1),\ \ R_{2}=(0,w^{5},1),\ \ P=(1,w^{26}+e,1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>26</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}=(0,w^{4},1),\ \ R_{2}=(0,w^{5},1),\ \ P=(1,w^{26}+e,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmexample2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=(w^{11}+w^{24}\delta,w^{16}+w^{29}\delta,1),\ \ P_{2}=(w^{15}+w^{8}\delta,w^{20}+w^{13}\delta,1),\ \ M=(w^{15}+\delta,w^{4}+w^{29}\delta,1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>24</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>29</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>20</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>13</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>29</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=(w^{11}+w^{24}\delta,w^{16}+w^{29}\delta,1),\ \ P_{2}=(w^{15}+w^{8}\delta,w^{20}+w^{13}\delta,1),\ \ M=(w^{15}+\delta,w^{4}+w^{29}\delta,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Computation shows that no O’Nan configuration contained in the Tits unital constructed by Feng and Li for the case <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=128</annotation></semantics></math> extends to a Fano plane.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Firstly, consider the non-classical orthogonal BM unitals of even order.
The O’Nans of Feng and Li have a line which contains the special point of the unital. We have shown their construction easily extends to a Fano plane contained in the unital, and consequently, contain an O’Nan configuration whose lines do not contain the special point. Further, we show that the number of these BM-special Fano planes in an orthogonal BM-unital depends only on the order of the unital, that is, it is the same for inequivalent orthogonal BM-unitals of the same even order.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that by our calculations using Magma <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> we can find BM-ordinary Fano planes for small values of <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, however is is an open conjecture whether these exist for all even <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider the Tits unital. In this case computations have shown that the O’Nan configurations of Feng and Li complete to a Fano plane for <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=8,32,512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=8,32,512</annotation></semantics></math>, and does not for <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=128</annotation></semantics></math>. Separate computations have shown however, that Fano planes exists in the Tits unital for <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=128</annotation></semantics></math> which necessarily is not one arising from the construction of Feng and Li.</p>
</div>
</section>
